instead of splitting it. let's change the structure of the json so that it makes sense inline.  for example:
```
{
    "dateLabel": "Date", // straight translation string
    "datePlaceholder": {
        "string": "yyyy-mm-dd",
        "verbatim": "allow" // all languages can be verbatim
    }
}
```
or:
```
{
    "dateLabel": "Date", // straight translation string
    "datePlaceholder": {
        "string": "yyyy-mm-dd",
        "verbatim": {
            "allow": [
                ["en", "en-US", "en*"],
                ["pt*"]
            ],
            "warn": ["ca", "es"],
            "error": ["*"]
        }
    }
}
```
we should be able to send just the strings and parse the return. don't use this structure strictly, use a best practice for a well defined pipeline.

